 "variant": "Empires of the Crossroads \u2014 Rome, Byzantium, Armenia, Persia, Iberia, Albania, Egypt (historic what-if)",
 "source": "Original map data created for Backstabplomacy for Raphael's Armenian church play group. A church-group sandbox: empires from different centuries meet on one board \u2014 it is a what-if, not a history exam. Armenia was the first nation to adopt Christianity (301 AD, under Tiridates III, evangelised by St Gregory the Illuminator); Ani was famed as the City of 1001 Churches; Jerusalem starts neutral and is worth exactly one centre like everywhere else \u2014 but watch what your friends will pay for it. Caucasian Albania (no relation to Balkan Albania) and Iberia (no relation to Spain) are the forgotten Christian kingdoms of the Caucasus, restored here to playable glory.",
